 "result_line": "Criterion 12 is PASS for all five GH1 families: every checker and owner-schema row their complete calls evaluate is CLOSED (gated PASS on real vectors plus a killed witness of that family) or CLOSED_BY_PROOF.",
 "standalone_other": "the private audit finds no isolated negative for `goal.progressed` `$defs/goal_status/type` (every non-string status also fails the status-pair oneOf), and the EventRecord nullable `project_id` anyOf is masked by the application-scope then-type: the same two-clause class. In the gated sweep these pairs are declared duplicate sets, with their joint and per-site cuts recorded in the ledger.",
 "evidence_text": "Bundle `/mnt/Cursor/PuppetMaster-Evidence/event-authority-20261104/drafts/PNC019/c12-gh1/`; `SHA256SUMS` pins every file.\n- `run/`: pass 1 (generation) collection and ledger.\n- `run/proof/`: pass 2 and the gated proof: collection, uncapped ledger, invalid mutations, mutations, signatures, family rows, schema inventory, source bindings (no drift), fabricated-row self-test, table summary and rows, and `gated-reports.tar.gz` with every tool report.\n- `supplement/`: the declared progressed supplement (same code and tables).\n- `coverage-matrix.json`: the full matrix.\n- `selftests/`: judge, numbers and contrast runs.\n- `standalone/`: before and after replays.\n- `tools/`: drivers, builders and the bundle script.\n\nRepository files: `reports/event-authority-20261115/PNC019-C12-GH1-core.json` (compact result, quoted by the cells), `PNC019-C12-GH1-coverage.json` (compact matrix), `PNC019-C12-GH1-grades.json` (five rows), `PNC019-C12-GH1.md` (this report).\n\nReplay (12 GB free first, then the 2 GB no-swap scope, as a long-job):\n```sh\ntools/run-full.sh OUT        # pm_goal_guard_sweep.py --generate --replace-generated --prove-generated --no-fuzz, ten sources\npython3 scripts/pm_goal_guard_sweep.py --no-fuzz --no-keyword-witnesses --source pm_goal_c12_supplement --out SUP\npython3 scripts/pm_goal_c12_matrix.py OUT/proof --family goal.child_status_changed --family goal.degraded \\\n  --family goal.progressed --family goal.replanned --family goal.scheduled --extra-ledger SUP/ledger.json.gz --out matrix.json\npython3 scripts/pm_goal_guard_sweep.py --judge-self-test --out DIR\npython3 scripts/pm_event_numbers.py --self-test --scope numbers\ntools/standalone-final.sh    # ATS-1119, ATS-210/212/213, ATS-211 (PM_GOAL_AUDIT_WORKERS=4)\npython3 scripts/pm-pnc019-s3a-grade-check.py reports/event-authority-20261115/PNC019-C12-GH1-grades.json\n```\nEvery heavy command ran with at least 12 GB available, under `systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=2G -p MemorySwapMax=0`, as a long-job. Code commit `c3d89a7d57`.",
 "for_jared": "Nothing to decide. No product choice came up, and no new test files were added (card E10-2 is unaffected).\n- The repository-wide date-time inventory stays NOT_RUN (C12-DC1-DTGATE-ROTATION, merge-2 integration).\n- s3ao's C12 cells for the other eight Goal families do not stand until GH2 and GO re-grade them.\n- Lane GC's two common-module defects are fixed on this branch (pushed for GC at `82df91325e`).\n- ATS-210's two remaining private-audit rows (`goal_run.certified`) belong to that suite's owner. They need a oneOf-only negative and an entailment note for the enum, not a common-module change.",
